  "news": {
    "title": "The Grasshopper — NZ forecast",
    "summary": "First up, Monday and Tuesday will be mostly fine, giving us a couple of decent days on the slopes before things turn wild and woolly. A slow-moving front rolls onto the lower South Island early Wednesday, with rain and high-level snow gradually turning to widespread snowfall as cold southerlies creep north. By Thursday, the Southern Lakes should wake to 20-40+cm of freshies and clearing skies, with Canterbury following suit later in the day. Wax the powder skis, it’s going to be epic!",
    "url": "https://www.mountainwatch.com/grasshopper/",
