      "summary": "Cardrona is open for skiing today, with 0 cm of new snow overnight or in the last 24 hours and excellent spring coverage across the mountain. The morning is firm and fast, with the groomers laying down fresh cord before the snow softens under the sun; some pockets of cold, dry snow remain in shaded upper sections. Current conditions are 2°C with 23 km/h winds and gusts to 39 km/h, with high cloud building later and NW winds increasing, which may affect operations in the afternoon. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express, Willow’s Quad and Wells Pipe Platter are all open. Learners Slopes, Main Basin, Captains, Soho, Little Willows, Big Willows, Ski Touring Access, Mt Cardrona, Arcadia Chutes and Summit are open. (Issued: 10:17 am, 15 Sep) Baby Bucks, Little Bucks, Antlers Alley, Stag Lane, Big Bucks, Peoples Pipe, Big Air and Gravity Cross are open, while Olympic Pipe is closed; the pipe is scheduled to close at 10:15am today, with the platter remaining open for Big Air. The Schools Alpine Race is being held on Upper Goldrush this morning. The access road is chain-free, but chains must be carried, with an active road-hazard advisory in place. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
